nce mid-September shows Brown ahead in every survey, with margins ranging from 3 to 8 points, and aggregated estimates put his lead near 4-5 points. Prediction markets price Brown's chances around 58-65 percent.\n\nBrown has dramatically outraised Husted, though outside groups have spent heavily against him. Husted benefits from Ohio's Republican-leaning electorate and presidential backing, including a Trump rally, but his appointee status limits traditional incumbency advantages. The race remains close enough that late campaign dynamics could decide it.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7221, "margin": 2.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7246, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6986, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6393, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6851, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7568, "margin": 3.5}]}